The Go rendering: one command module whose command calls one function of a
package, beside two dead exported functions of that package that call one
unexported function, and a third dead exported function that calls nothing.
Every function spans one line. Nothing in the module imports anything outside
it, so the rendering loads with no network access.

-- fixture.json --
{
  "symbols": {
    "Live": { "file": "target/pair/pair.go", "line": 4 },
    "Left": { "file": "target/pair/pair.go", "line": 7 },
    "Right": { "file": "target/pair/pair.go", "line": 10 },
    "shared": { "file": "target/pair/pair.go", "line": 13 },
    "Alone": { "file": "target/pair/pair.go", "line": 16 }
  }
}
-- target/go.mod --
module example.com/target

go 1.27.0
-- target/main.go --
package main

import "example.com/target/pair"

func main() { println(pair.Live()) }
-- target/pair/pair.go --
package pair

// Live is called by the command.
func Live() int { return 1 }

// Left is called by nothing.
func Left() int { return shared() }

// Right is called by nothing.
func Right() int { return shared() + 1 }

// shared is called by Left and Right alone.
func shared() int { return 4 }

// Alone is called by nothing and calls nothing.
func Alone() int { return 5 }
